## Pour sequence

Pour basket by basket, high to low raw uL within each basket:

1. **BASKET 1 — Always used:** Hedione (500), Iso E Super (130).
2. **BASKET 2 — Vetivers:** Vetival (80), Vetikon (60), Indian Vetiver EO (50).
3. **BASKET 3 — Woods:** Sandalwood EO (240), Sandalore (170), Polysantol (130), Ebanol (100), Suederal (100), Cedramber (80), Kephalis (80), Cabreuva EO (80), Azarbre (70), Nerolidol (60), Cypress EO (50), Cedarwood EO (50), Javanol (50), Timberol (50), Himalayan Cedarwood EO (40), Patchouli EO (30), Nagarmortha Oil (20), Cade Oil Rectified (20).
4. **BASKET 4 — Wood modifiers and ambers:** Vertofix (90), Cashmeran (80), Ambrofix (70), Amberwood F (50), Ambermax (50), Norlimbanol Dextro (40), Elemi EO (40).
5. **BASKET 5 — Wood-vetivers:** Koavone (70).
6. **BASKET 6 — Musks:** Ambrettolide (330).
7. **BASKET 7 — Muguet and lavender:** Florol (240), Helional (50), Nympheal (50), Lilyreal ND (45), Mayol (40), Linalyl Acetate (40), Freesia HDI (35), Linalool (30), Hydroxycitronellol (30), Bourgeonal (25), Cyclamen Aldehyde (20).
8. **BASKET 8 — Jasmine, indole, and magnolia:** Magnolia EO (680), Jasmine Absolute (330), Benzyl Acetate (240), Methyl Benzoate (100), Phenyl Ethyl Acetate (80), Dihydrojasmone (60), PEDMC (60), Benzyl Alcohol (60), Jessemal (50), Indole (40), Stralyl Acetate (30), Nerol (30), Cis Jasmone (20), Petitgrain EO (20), Farnesol (20).
9. **BASKET 9 — Ylang, orange flower, and narcotics:** Tuberose Absolute (300), Neroli EO (240), Hexyl Salicylate (220), Benzyl Salicylate (200), Aurantiol (150), Methyl Salicylate (60), Terpinyl Acetate (40), Nerolin Bromelia (40), Oranger Crystals (40), ACA (40), Benzaldehyde (20).
10. **BASKET 10 — Rose:** Phenethyl Alcohol (180), Citronellol (20), Geraniol (20).
11. **BASKET 15 — Fruits:** Damascol (25), Damascenone (20).
12. **BASKET 16 — Aldehydes:** Adoxal (20).
13. **BASKET 17 — Green smelling things:** Parmavert (40), Verdyl Acetate (20), Cis-3-Hexenol (20).

Stir after each basket. Add 22.80 mL ethanol only after the 7,200 uL concentrate is complete.

**Current-build reference:** `formula:white-fire-reliquary:current:v2`  
**Inventory authority date:** 2026-08-27.  
**Buildability:** identity/stock-list buildable. Quantity, lot authenticity,
safety, stability, performance, and sensory success remain unverified.

## 5. Missing-chemical and authority impact gate

| Item | State | Impact | Required handling |
|---|---|---|---|
| Formula chemical identities | `NO_MISSING_CHEMICAL` | all 78 target identities map to live inventory | no procurement recommendation |
| White Champi lot identity, amount, plant part, extraction | `HOLD_LOT_AND_QUANTITY` | failure blocks the named lead and may invalidate natural-OAV assumptions | bind label photographs, supplier, lot, remaining volume, and documentation before any physical batch |
| White Champi COA / GC-MS / GC-O | `HOLD_COMPOSITE_OAV` | strict lot-specific composition and realism diagnostics unavailable | preserve whole-natural identity and do not invent a monomolecular Magnolia OAV |
| White Champi SDS / IFRA / allergen data | `HOLD_SAFETY` | no skin or release decision possible | obtain current supplier documents before skin work |
| Other natural lots | `LOT_GENERALIZATION_LIMIT` | repository decompositions are literature proxies, not bottle truth | report composite model provenance and retain lot uncertainty |
| Free Methyl Anthranilate with aldehydes | `REMOVED_PREMIX` | the prior free-amine row created an avoidable Schiff-base/reaction risk | current v2 uses Terpinyl Acetate plus bounded Aurantiol; no equivalence claim |
| Formula-row safety and compatibility | `HOLD_PHYSICAL_REVIEW` | high row resolution still creates precipitation/oxidation and restricted-material questions | run current IFRA/allergen and physical-chemistry review before any compounding authorization |

**Purchase recommendation:** none. Documentation requests are recommended, but
this file authorizes neither procurement nor physical preparation.

